      "text": "To solve the given problem, we need to evaluate each term separately and then sum the results. The expression is:\n\n\\[\n\\left\\lceil\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\right\\rceil+\\left\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\rceil+\\left\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\right\\rceil\n\\]\n\n**Step-by-step evaluation:**\n\n1. **Evaluate \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{9}}{\\sqrt{4}} = \\frac{3}{2} = 1.5\n   \\]\n   The ceiling of \\(1.5\\) is:\n   \\[\n   \\left\\lceil 1.5 \\right\\rceil = 2\n   \\]\n\n2. **Evaluate \\(\\frac{9}{4}\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{9}{4} = 2.25\n   \\]\n   The ceiling of \\(2.25\\) is:\n   \\[\n   \\left\\lceil 2.25 \\right\\rceil = 3\n   \\]\n\n3. **Evaluate \\(\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2 = \\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right) \\times \\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right) = \\frac{81}{16} = 5.0625\n   \\]\n   The ceiling of \\(5.0625\\) is:\n   \\[\n   \\left\\lceil 5.0625 \\right\\rceil = 6\n   \\]\n\nNow, we sum the results of the ceiling evaluations:\n\\[\n\\left\\lceil\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\right\\rceil+\\left\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\rceil+\\left\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\right\\rceil = 2 + 3 + 6 = 11\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{11}\n\\]",
